      "provenance": {
        "kind": "handwritten",
        "rationale": "The proposal's own worked example, ported and brought up to the landed account plane. Two things changed since 4.3 was written and both are recorded rather than hidden: the transition now carries a seventh account, the SupplyLedgerAccount, and the identities in 4.3's table are not reproducible because canonical_profile_hash now requires exactly 64 preimage bytes. The identities here are the real derivations for the canonical 64-byte parent profile preimage with realm nonce 7 and market nonce 9. The closed single-position model refuses before the kernel runs: the ledger says one internal atom of outcome 0 exists, and the kernel aggregate says zero. Metadata, bindings, bumps, links, padding, replay sequence, and signature are all valid, so closure is the only fault.",
        "source": "docs/implementation/VECTOR_SPINE_PROPOSAL.md#43"
      },
      "status": "proposed",
      "surface": "solana-reference",
      "title": "a forged position cannot materialize claims absent from aggregate supply"
    },
    {
      "comparison": {
        "byte_exact": "not-applicable",
        "post_state_on_error": "unchanged",
        "precedence_note": "apply_inner runs validate_metadata, Request::decode, account decode, validate_links, validate_padding, validate_aggregate_closure, and the replay sequence check before it dispatches on the action; the Resolve and RedeemInternal arms then take `evidence.ok_or(ResolutionEvidenceUnavailable)` as their first statement, before any signature, authority, terms, window, or payout-index check. Step 2 therefore carries a second latent fault (payout index 9 is outside the payout set) that the evidence gate strictly precedes.",
        "semantic": true,
        "single_fault": false
      },
