      "provenance": {
        "kind": "handwritten",
        "rationale": "`apply` supplies no evidence plane, so the fail-closed default is the absence of a code path rather than a flag anybody can set. Step 2 uses an out-of-range payout index deliberately: the refusal is still the evidence class and not a shape class, because the evidence gate precedes every payout-set read. This is the by_design refusal of TAX-5, and weakening it to make an integration test pass is exactly what AGENTS.md forbids.",
